      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the error you mentioned in https://crbug.com/377820810#comment20 is because now every `BindGroupLayoutEntry` defaults to `{Uniform,BindingNotUsed,BindingNotUsed,BindingNotUsed}` instead of `{BindingNotUsed,BindingNotUsed,BindingNotUsed,BindingNotUsed}`.\n\nThere are some limitations with the generator because it just has one concept of \"default\" but what we want is three different \"defaults\" depending on what you\u0027re asking:\n1. webgpu_cpp.h `BindGroupLayoutEntry::buffer \u003d { nullptr, BindingNotUsed, false, 0 }`\n2. webgpu_cpp.h `BufferBindingLayout::type \u003d Undefined` \n3. wgpu_structs_autogen.cpp `BufferBindingLayout::WithTrivialFrontendDefaults()` should apply defaulting (`Undefined` -\u003e `Uniform`).\n\nHowever the second one, changing the C/C++ defaults to `Undefined` instead of their trivial defaults, is a broader change to the entire C/C++ APIs that we\u0027ll want to deal with separately.\n\nRight now, we should skip that part, and have:\n2. webgpu_cpp.h `BufferBindingLayout.type \u003d Uniform` \n\nas you have done here. The thing that needs to be fixed for it to work correctly is item 1. There may also be some downstream dependencies that are setting `.buffer \u003d {}` instead of leaving it default-initialized, and if so we\u0027ll need to update them.",
      "range": {
