      "message": "yes. In the upstream webgpu-headers C header I used zero-initialization as a shortcut to set everything to BindingNotUsed in WGPUBindGroupLayoutEntry. However in C++ this is [not possible](https://stackoverflow.com/a/61240590) so instead I think the easiest thing is to have a special case in the code generation. Either:\n- Add `wgpu::BindGroupLayoutEntry` to [SpecialStructures](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/generator/templates/api_cpp.h;l\u003d709;drc\u003d9e1b2d56b85a4908388b5614ac66bbcc9bf3b5fa) and manually define it\n- Put some special case in [`render_cpp_default_value`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/generator/templates/api_cpp.h;l\u003d742;drc\u003d9e1b2d56b85a4908388b5614ac66bbcc9bf3b5fa) (or somewhere) so it sets the appropriate defaults for each of these fields.",
